      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Logic: </span><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">(</span></mo><mtext><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">first number</span></mtext><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">)</span></mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">(</span></mo><mtext><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">second number</span></mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">)  <span style=\"font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400;\">= pattern that gives </span><span data-end=\"87\" data-start=\"81\" style=\"font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: bolder;\">64</span><span style=\"font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400;\">.  </span></span></mo></mrow></msup></mrow></semantics></math></span></span>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">So, </span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">4 @ 3 = 64</span> is odd from the rest given.</span></p>\n",
