n></span></span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-381\" style=\"font-family: MathJax_Main; padding-left: 0.301em;\">=</span><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-382\" style=\"font-family: MathJax_Main; padding-left: 0.301em;\">9</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></nobr><span class=\"MJX_Assistive_MathML\" role=\"presentation\"> <script id=\"MathJax-Element-10\" type=\"math/mml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>, 3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></semantics></math></script> </span></span> <script id=\"MathJax-Element-45\" type=\"math/mml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>, 3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></semantics></math></script> </span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Thus,  the required fraction is: <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">256 / 9.</span></p>\n",
