      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Total heads = 30</p>\n\n<p>and Total legs = 94</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>Assume all 30 animals have at least 2 legs:</p>\n\n<p>30 heads&nbsp;x 2 legs&nbsp;= 60 legs.</p>\n\n<p>Find the &quot;extra&quot; legs: The problem says there are 94 legs.</p>\n\n<p>So, 94 - 60 = 34&nbsp;extra legs.</p>\n\n<p>Assign the extra legs:</p>\n\n<p>These 34 legs must belong to the dogs (since they have 2 more legs than hens).</p>\n\n<p>Each dog takes 2 extra legs.</p>\n\n<p>Number of dogs: 34 &divide;&nbsp;2 = 17 dogs.</p>\n\n<p>Number of <span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">hens</span>: 30 heads&nbsp;- 17&nbsp;dogs&nbsp;= 13 hens.</p>\n\n<p>Thus, there are&nbsp;13 hens.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hence, the correct answer is &#39;Option 3&#39;.</strong></p>\n",
